Conclusion: NO-OP port for SI conversion. Admin pages are infrastructure /
control surfaces (system health, audit logs, API keys, backup configs,
dev tools, request builder, log viewers, RBAC matrix, signal viewer,
security events). They render bytes (file_size), milliseconds
(duration_ms), HTTP counts, status enums, JSON payloads, and timestamps
— none of which are physical-unit quantities that need °C↔°F or m↔mi
conversion. Same outcome pattern as Phase-43/0024 (telemetry),
Phase-43/0031 (automations), and Phase-43/0032 (notifications).

=== HOOK_PORT ===
useAdmin.ts (web/src/api/hooks/useAdmin.ts):

CHANGE 1: useStateTimeline marked @deprecated.
  Phase-42 / Prompt 0077 removed the `/vehicle-states/timeline` route
  alongside the `vehicle_states` table drop. Endpoint now returns 404.
  Hook retained because the out-of-scope dashboard widget
  `features/dashboard/widgets/DashboardStatsWidget.tsx` still imports
  it; useQuery surfaces the 404 gracefully via `error` per ADR-005 #1.
  A future replacement should derive state-duration timelines from the
  canonical `fsm_transitions` table instead.
  Locked-policy continuation from Phase-43 prompts 0023 + 0024 + 0025 +
  0026 + 0027 + 0029 + 0030 + 0031 + 0032.

NO OTHER HOOK CHANGES. Justification:
  - All other URLs verified ALIVE against router.go (see PREFLIGHT).
  - All URLs already conform to no-`/api/v1/`-prefix rule (auto-prefixed
    by request() in api/client.ts).
  - All query params already snake_case (vehicle_id, page, limit, days).
  - Hook return types use legacy interfaces from `@/types/admin` (not
    `@/api/types`) because the api/types.ts variants are STRUCTURALLY
    DIFFERENT shapes: legacy uses camelCase + Date|null while api/types
    uses snake_case + different field sets (e.g. APICallLog gains `ts`,
    `service`, `http_method`, `endpoint`, `status_code`, `duration_ms`,
    `error_message`, `rate_limited` — vs legacy `id`, `method`, `url`,
    `statusCode`, `durationMs`, `requestBody`, `responseBody`, `error`,
    `createdAt`). Switching the hook to api/types would break every
    in-scope page (AdminPage, APIKeysPage, ApiLogsPage, BackupRestore,
    SecurityAccessPage, MaintenanceModePanel) AND every out-of-scope
    consumer (12 dashboard widgets + system pages + MaintenanceBanner)
    on field-access TS errors. The locked-policy precedent applies:
    when api/types reconciliation would break runtime field access on
    out-of-scope consumers, defer the type unification to a coordinated
    cross-cutting prompt rather than break callers in this scope.
  - At runtime, `camelCaseKeys` in lib/resilience.ts:19-34 retains BOTH
    snake_case (Go JSON tag) AND camelCase variants on every response
    object, so the legacy camelCase types match wire shape exactly.

=== PAGE_PORT ===
NO PAGE SOURCE EDITS. Justification per page (in-scope features/admin/):

  AdminPage.tsx — Renders system health status, component count, DB
    size string ("X MB"), table count, audit log search, API-key list,
    maintenance panel. All values are infrastructure metadata. No SI
    quantities. Imports `useRefreshAuth` from useSettings (admin-auth
    helper) — NOT user-pref `useSettings()`. No SI conversion needed.

  APIKeysPage.tsx — CRUD over /api-keys; renders name, permission
    badges, masked key prefix, expires_at date. No SI quantities.

  ApiLogsPage.tsx — Renders API call log entries (method, URL, status
    code, duration_ms, request/response body) and stats (totals, error
    rate, average duration). No SI quantities.

  ApiPlaygroundPage.tsx — Interactive request builder; renders raw
    JSON request/response payloads. No SI quantities.

  BackupRestorePage.tsx — CRUD over /backup/configs and /backup/runs;
    renders backup type, frequency days, retention count, file_size
    in bytes, duration_ms. No SI quantities.

  DevToolsPage.tsx — Tooling shell hosting per-tool sub-components
    (HashCalculator, JsonFormatter, RegexTester, etc.). No SI
    quantities at the page level.

  FeedbackQueuePage.tsx — Renders admin feedback rows (subject, body,
    submitter, status). No SI quantities.

  FleetAPIPage.tsx — Polling-config toggles for Tesla Fleet API
    endpoints. The "odometer/locks/doors" strings are i18n LABELS
    describing endpoint coverage, not telemetry values. No SI
    quantities.

  LiveLogsPage.tsx — SSE log tail viewer. Renders log lines as raw
    text. No SI quantities.

  RbacMatrixPage.tsx — Permission matrix grid. No SI quantities.

  RedisSignalViewerPage.tsx — Raw Redis HSET viewer for live signals.
    The signal-NAME prefix regex categorises (Driving/Battery/Climate/
    etc.) but does NOT convert signal VALUES — the viewer is a debug
    tool that shows raw stored values verbatim. SI conversion would
    actually be HARMFUL here (would obscure the wire data the operator
    is debugging).

  SecurityAccessPage.tsx — Renders security-event timeline (locked,
    sentry_mode, door/window state, lights, etc.). All boolean / enum
    values. No SI quantities.

  SystemPage.tsx — Page shell. No SI quantities.

  UsersPage.tsx — User list with email + ForwardAuth subject. No SI
    quantities.

NO `=== UNPORTABLE ===` block — every page is portable AS-IS because
no SI conversion is applicable.

=== I18N ===
NO i18n CHANGES. No new strings introduced (no page edits). Existing
i18n keys preserved per never-delete-keys rule from Phase-43 prompt
0002.

