7. WINDOWS GATE QUIRKS reused (precedent: Phase-43/0021 + 0023 +
   0029 + 0030 + 0031 + 0032):
   (a) Resolve-Path absolute on $log BEFORE any Push-Location, else
       Tee-Object loses the file under `web/.github/...` during BUILD.
   (b) `.\node_modules\.bin\tsc.cmd` and `npm.cmd run build` instead
       of `npx tsc` / `npm run build` to dodge npm 10's executable
       resolution quirk under `pwsh -File` invocation.
   (c) Self-deleting gate script via Remove-Item before the git-status
       check, else `.tmp_gate_0033.ps1` trips the disallowed-file
       check.
   (d) git status --porcelain parsed by Substring(3) instead of regex
       on the status line, because [regex]::Escape on a Windows-style
       backslash path doesn't match git's forward-slash porcelain
       output. `-like "$prefix*"` matches forward-slash paths.

